course: dictionary
lesson: 12273
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Contracted is one of them. The words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning fits. «The metal contracted as it cooled.» Things get smaller when they cool, so here contracted means became smaller.
explain: «She contracted measles last week.» You do not shrink from measles. You catch the illness, so contracted here means caught. The same word can mean something very different in another sentence.
explain: «The firm was contracted to build the new bridge.» A firm is a company, and a bridge is not built by accident. The company agreed in writing to do the work, so here contracted means made a formal agreement. Always try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Contracted can mean became smaller or shorter, as in «The metal contracted as it cooled».
fact: Contracted can mean caught an illness, as in «She contracted measles».
fact: Contracted can mean made a formal agreement to do work, as in «The firm was contracted to build the bridge».
fact: In grammar, a contracted form is a word shortened by joining two words, such as «don't» for «do not» or «it's» for «it is».
fact: When you meet a word with more than one meaning, check the words around it to find the right one.
exercise: «The metal contracted as it cooled.» In this sentence, what does contracted mean? | Made a promise to build | Caught a cold | Grew bigger and wider | *Became smaller
exercise: «She contracted measles last week and stayed in bed.» What did she do? | Shortened a word | *Caught an illness | Got smaller | Signed a contract for work
exercise: «Don't is a contracted form of do not.» What is contracted here? | *Shortened by joining two words | Agreed to do a job | Became smaller in size | Caught a germ
test: «The firm was contracted to build the new bridge.» What does contracted mean here? | Cooled down | Caught a fever | Became shorter | *Agreed in writing to do the work
test: Which sentence uses contracted as a grammar word? | *«It's» is a contracted form of «it is» | «She contracted a cold» | «The firm was contracted to clean the school» | «The ice contracted in the freezer»
exam: Sam says «Muscles contract to move your bones.» What does contract mean there? | Grow longer and thinner | Sign a deal to move the bones | *Become shorter and tighter, pulling the bones | Forget how to move
